316
00:45:55,940 --> 00:46:03,220
And in teaching and learning programming languages in general, historically,

317
00:46:05,844 --> 00:46:17,564
Structured programming has been invented first and then object-oriented programming has been proposed.

318
00:46:18,903 --> 00:46:26,804
And moreover, object-oriented programming is a superset of procedural structural programming.

319
00:46:27,219 --> 00:46:36,799
An object by itself works according to structural programming principles.

320
00:46:37,900 --> 00:46:48,920
And on top of that, it obeys to object-oriented rules within itself and with its interactions with other objects.

321
00:46:54,643 --> 00:47:09,763
According to the volume of the knowledge, most universities and programming courses first teach structural programming, then they teach object-to-react program.

322
00:47:09,763 --> 00:47:20,943
This is the dominant approach for education, but the other way around is also possible.

323
00:47:21,492 --> 00:47:30,791
Without learning structured programming, you can begin with the basic principles and applications of object orientation.

324
00:47:31,315 --> 00:47:39,715
Then you continue with structured programming concepts such as control, flow, decision-making, loops, etc.

325
00:47:40,576 --> 00:47:48,396
And then you can continue with other more advanced concepts of object orientation.

326
00:47:49,115 --> 00:47:54,115
This second approach is called object-first approach.

327
00:47:54,512 --> 00:48:02,211
And the traditional one is called structured first approach.

328
00:48:03,211 --> 00:48:18,211
Both approaches can be successful and objects first approach has been applied, has been used successfully in even...

329
00:48:18,867 --> 00:48:31,788
